            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic gastric pancreatitis: unusual cause of epigastric pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>295-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ectopic pancreatic tissue has the same characteristics than normal pancreatic tissue.Therefore it may be affected by the same diseases. We report a rare cause of epigastric pain due to gastric heterotopic pancreatitis.The rare diagnosis was suspected by ultrasound and CT and definitively confirmed by echo-endoscopic guided biopsies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
